---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Snippet from '../components/Snippet.astro';
import HostStartTabs from '../components/HostStartTabs.astro';
import Pipeline from '../components/Pipeline.astro';
import LessonOutline from '../components/LessonOutline.astro';
import RepoLinks from '../components/RepoLinks.astro';
import { path } from '../lib/url';
import { FIRST_LESSON } from '../lib/lessons';
---

<Marketing>
    <Hero />

    <section class="section-intro proof-section" aria-labelledby="s-proof">
        <p class="kicker">/00 - why</p>
        <h2 id="s-proof">What you get</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            Reach for SJON when JSON gets in the author's way but a
            full language would give them too much. You get the shared
            document machinery a homegrown DSL usually has to rebuild
            anyway: parsing, validation, formatting, diagnostics, editing,
            and interchange. All of it ready to plug into your tool.
        </p>

        <div class="proof-grid">
            <article class="card card--main proof-card">
                <div class="card__deck">
                    <div class="card__panel proof-panel">
                        <p class="kicker">files that read like the domain</p>
                        <h3>The file looks like the thing it describes.</h3>
                        <p>
                            Each <code>(name ...)</code> group names the
                            thing it describes. The <code>:words</code>
                            inside are its fields. Units stay attached to
                            their numbers, so authors aren't poking
                            around nested objects wondering which field is
                            which.
                        </p>
                        <Snippet bare code={`(camera
  :mode ortho
  :zoom 2
  :delay 4b)`} />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card card--main proof-card">
                <div class="card__deck">
                    <div class="card__panel proof-panel">
                        <p class="kicker">errors that point at the typo</p>
                        <h3>When something is off, your app can say so.</h3>
                        <p>
                            Schemas describe the forms and slots your app
                            accepts. A misspelled key becomes a precise
                            diagnostic with a span and a suggestion,
                            not a vague parse failure.
                        </p>
                        <div class="diagnostic" role="group" aria-label="Example SJON diagnostic">
                            <pre><code>{`error[unknown_key]:
(camera :mode ortho :zom 2)
                    ^^^^
note: Did you mean \`:zoom\`?`}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card card--main proof-card">
                <div class="card__deck">
                    <div class="card__panel proof-panel">
                        <p class="kicker">inline math, no runtime smuggled in</p>
                        <h3>Small calculations stay small.</h3>
                        <p>
                            Expressions only call the functions you allow.
                            Authors get inline math and helpers without
                            imports, <abbr title="Input/Output">I/O</abbr>, mutation, or recursion
                            sneaking in along with them.
                        </p>
                        <Snippet bare code={`:zoom (* 2 (b 1))
:alpha (smoothstep 0 1 t)
:seed  (hash scene-name 4)`} />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-intro start-section" aria-labelledby="s-start">
        <p class="kicker">/01 - start</p>
        <h2 id="s-start">Start by reading the file</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            Get a feel for SJON the way an author writes it: named
            forms, keyword slots, units, comments, and small inline math.
            The same source text parses identically from Zig, JavaScript,
            or Rust, so your editor and your runtime agree.
        </p>
        <HostStartTabs />
        <p class="start-more">
            Prefer a guided path? <a href={path(FIRST_LESSON.route)}>Take the tutorial</a>. Already wiring it up?
            Jump to
            <a href="https://git.hugodaniel.com/releases/sjon#consuming">README &sect; Consuming</a>
            or
            <a href="https://git.hugodaniel.com/releases/sjon/src/branch/main/docs/AUTHORING.md">AUTHORING.md</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card card--main card--no-stripes prose-card" aria-labelledby="s-model">
        <div class="card__deck">
            <div class="card__panel prose">
                <p class="kicker">/02 - model</p>
                <h2 id="s-model">The whole model in 30 seconds</h2>
                <p>
                    A SJON document is a tree built from a small set of
                    pieces: forms, vectors, keywords, symbols, strings,
                    booleans, nil, plain numbers, and numbers that carry a
                    unit. The form below is small, but it touches
                    most of that surface:
                </p>

                <Snippet bare code={`(camera :mode ortho :zoom 2 :delay 4b :pos [(* 2 1920) 1080])`} />

                <ul class="fact-list">
                    <li>
                        <strong>Forms are constructors.</strong>
                        <span><code>(camera ...)</code> is just data
                        until a schema says what <code>camera</code> means
                        and which fields it accepts.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Keywords are slots or flags.</strong>
                        <span><code>:mode ortho</code> and <code>:zoom 2</code>
                        are key/value pairs; a lone <code>:loop</code>
                        would be a positional flag.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Expressions are opt-in.</strong>
                        <span><code>(* 2 1920)</code> only runs when the
                        host has explicitly allowed <code>*</code>. Inside
                        a vector it sits next to literals like any other
                        value.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Units survive every hop.</strong>
                        <span><code>4b</code> stays a four-beat duration
                        through printing, JSON, and binary <abbr title="Intermediate Representation">IR</abbr>. Same
                        for <code>90deg</code>, <code>50%</code>, and
                        <code>250ms</code>.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="compare-teaser card card--main card--no-stripes" aria-labelledby="s-compare">
        <div class="card__deck">
            <div class="card__panel compare-teaser__panel">
                <div>
                    <p class="kicker">/03 - compare</p>
                    <h2 id="s-compare">Why not just JSON or <abbr title="Extensible Data Notation">EDN</abbr>?</h2>
                    <p>
                        JSON is still the best thing to send across the
                        wire. SJON is what you reach for <em>before</em> that:
                        the source file someone is actually editing, with
                        comments, symbolic names, schema diagnostics, safe
                        expressions, and lossless round trips.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <a class="compare-link" href={path('/compare')}>
                    <span>See the side-by-side</span>
                    <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-intro proof-section" aria-labelledby="s-agents">
        <p class="kicker">/04 - agents</p>
        <h2 id="s-agents">The other author</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            A growing share of config isn't typed by a person anymore
            &mdash; it's generated by a model and reviewed by one. SJON
            treats that author as first-class: hand it the schema, let it
            write the document, and the validator answers with something
            it can act on. Generate, validate, repair. The same loop the
            tutorial teaches humans runs fine without one. Point a model
            at <a href={path('/llms.txt')}>llms.txt</a> to prime it on the
            whole language in a couple thousand tokens.
        </p>

        <div class="proof-grid">
            <article class="card card--main proof-card">
                <div class="card__deck">
                    <div class="card__panel proof-panel">
                        <p class="kicker">a contract that fits in a context window</p>
                        <h3>The schema is the prompt.</h3>
                        <p>
                            The schema is SJON too: one declaration that
                            says what every form is allowed to be. Paste it
                            into the prompt and the model has your domain's
                            grammar &mdash; and it can't drift from the
                            checker, because the checker reads the same
                            bytes.
                        </p>
                        <Snippet bare code={`(form :name camera
  (key :name mode
    :type symbol)
  (key :name zoom
    :type number))
; the model reads what
; the checker enforces`} />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card card--main proof-card">
                <div class="card__deck">
                    <div class="card__panel proof-panel">
                        <p class="kicker">errors a model can repair</p>
                        <h3>The error is the instruction.</h3>
                        <p>
                            A hundred-plus stable diagnostic codes, each
                            with a span and a semantic path. This isn't a
                            hint for a human squinting at a terminal
                            &mdash; it's an instruction an agent applies
                            and re-validates, unsupervised.
                        </p>
                        <div class="diagnostic" role="group" aria-label="Example SJON diagnostic an agent can act on">
                            <pre><code>{`error[unknown_key]:
(camera :mode ortho :zom 2)
                    ^^^^
note: Did you mean \`:zoom\`?`}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card card--main proof-card">
                <div class="card__deck">
                    <div class="card__panel proof-panel">
                        <p class="kicker">nothing to sandbox</p>
                        <h3>Generated SJON is read, never executed.</h3>
                        <p>
                            Expressions call only the functions you allow
                            &mdash; no imports, no <abbr title="Input/Output">I/O</abbr>,
                            no mutation, no recursion. Accepting
                            machine-written input costs exactly what
                            parsing data costs.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card card--main prose-card" aria-labelledby="s-architecture">
        <div class="card__deck">
            <div class="card__panel prose">
                <p class="kicker">/05 - architecture</p>
                <h2 id="s-architecture">Parse once, share the tree</h2>
                <p>
                    The parser builds one <abbr title="Structure of Arrays">SoA</abbr> <em>Ast.Tree</em>.
                    Validation, printing, JSON, binary IR, structural
                    edits, and expression evaluation all read from that
                    same tree, so every tool agrees on spans,
                    diagnostics, comments, and round trips by construction.
                </p>
                <Pipeline />
                <p>
                    Parsing SJON never turns a source file into a running
                    program. It reads data. No imports, no I/O, no
                    mutation, no recursion through user-defined code.
                </p>
                <p>
                    JSON stays the format you send to other systems. SJON
                    keeps the distinctions your tools care about while
                    someone is still editing the source: keyword vs symbol
                    vs string, unit-bearing numbers, comments, spans, and
                    original source order all the way through to binary
                    IR.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The package itself stops at shared document machinery:
                    parser, validator, printer, expression evaluator,
                    editor reducer, JSON bridge, and binary reader. Your
                    app stays in charge of what the words actually mean.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-intro keep-going-section" aria-labelledby="s-next">
        <p class="kicker">/06 - keep going</p>
        <h2 id="s-next">Keep going</h2>

        <h3 class="keep-going-heading">Take the tutorial</h3>
        <p class="lede">
            Start with a single <code>(scene ...)</code> and grow it: atoms,
            units, expressions, schemas, cross-references, and fixing things
            by reading the diagnostic. One small file at a time, no setup
            required.
        </p>
        <LessonOutline />

        <h3 class="keep-going-heading">Keep these tabs open</h3>
        <p class="lede">
            What to reach for while you wire SJON into a tool, sanity-check
            the 1.0 language surface, or look up anything from the examples
            on this page.
        </p>
        <RepoLinks />
    </section>
</Marketing>

<style>
    .prose-card {
        max-width: var(--landing-width);
        margin: var(--space-5) auto;
    }
    .prose {
        font-family: var(--body);
        color: var(--ink);
        padding: calc(var(--card-stripes-h) + var(--space-4)) var(--landing-inset) var(--space-5);
    }
    .prose h2 {
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: var(--step-2);
        letter-spacing: 0;
        margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
        color: var(--ink);
    }
    .prose p {
        font-size: var(--step-0);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        color: var(--ink);
        max-width: var(--measure);
    }
    .prose p + p { margin-top: 0.85em; }
    .prose code,
    .section-intro code {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.92em;
        font-weight: 500;
        background: var(--surface-mute);
        border: 1px solid var(--rule-mute);
        border-radius: 3px;
        padding: 1px 5px;
        color: var(--ink);
    }
    .prose em {
        font-style: italic;
        font-family: 'Iowan Old Style', 'Charter', 'Georgia', serif;
        color: var(--accent);
    }

    .section-intro {
        max-width: var(--landing-width);
        margin: var(--space-5) auto;
        padding: 0 var(--landing-inset);
    }
    .section-intro > .kicker,
    .prose > .kicker,
    .compare-teaser__panel > div > .kicker {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-size: 15px;
        line-height: 1.25;
        color: var(--accent);
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
        margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }
    .section-intro h2 {
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: var(--step-2);
        letter-spacing: 0;
        color: var(--ink);
        margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }
    .section-intro .lede {
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: var(--step-0);
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
        max-width: var(--measure);
    }

    .proof-section {
        max-width: var(--landing-width);
    }
    .proof-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: var(--space-3);
        align-items: start;
    }
    .proof-card {
        min-width: 0;
    }
    .proof-panel {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: var(--space-2);
        padding: calc(var(--card-stripes-h) + var(--space-3)) var(--space-3) var(--space-3);
    }
    .proof-panel .kicker {
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    .proof-panel h3 {
        font-size: 18px;
        line-height: 1.25;
        letter-spacing: 0;
    }
    .proof-panel p {
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        line-height: 1.5;
        font-size: 14.5px;
    }
    .proof-panel .snippet {
        margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
    }
    .proof-panel .snippet pre,
    .diagnostic pre {
        margin: 0;
        border: 1px solid var(--rule-mute);
        border-radius: 6px;
        overflow-x: auto;
        background: var(--surface-mute);
        padding: var(--space-3);
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 12.5px;
        font-weight: 500;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--ink);
    }
    .diagnostic {
        margin-top: var(--space-2);
    }

    .fact-list {
        display: grid;
        gap: var(--space-2);
        margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
    }
    .fact-list li {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr;
        gap: var(--space-3);
        padding-top: var(--space-2);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-mute);
    }
    .fact-list strong {
        font-size: 15px;
        color: var(--ink);
    }
    .fact-list span {
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .compare-teaser {
        max-width: var(--landing-width);
        margin: var(--space-5) auto;
    }
    .compare-teaser__panel {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
        gap: var(--space-4);
        align-items: end;
        padding: calc(var(--card-stripes-h) + var(--space-4)) var(--landing-inset) var(--space-5);
    }
    .compare-teaser h2 {
        font-size: var(--step-2);
        letter-spacing: 0;
        margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }
    .compare-teaser p:not(.kicker) {
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        max-width: 56ch;
    }
    .compare-link {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8px;
        white-space: nowrap;
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--surface);
        text-decoration: none;
        padding: 10px 16px;
        border-radius: var(--radius-card);
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 15px;
        box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--accent);
        transition: transform 0.12s ease, box-shadow 0.12s ease, background 0.12s ease;
    }
    .compare-link:hover {
        background: var(--accent);
        color: var(--surface);
        box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--ink);
        transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
    }

    .start-section {
        max-width: var(--landing-width);
        margin-top: var(--space-3);
    }
    .start-section .snippet { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); }
    .start-more {
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: 14px;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .start-more a {
        color: var(--ink);
        text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .keep-going-section { max-width: var(--landing-width); }
    .keep-going-section .keep-going-heading {
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 20px;
        letter-spacing: 0;
        color: var(--ink);
        margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-2);
    }
    .keep-going-section .keep-going-heading:first-of-type {
        margin-top: var(--space-3);
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
        .proof-grid {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .section-intro {
            margin: var(--space-4) auto;
        }
        .prose {
            padding: calc(var(--card-stripes-h) + var(--space-3)) var(--landing-inset) var(--space-3);
        }
        .fact-list li {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            gap: var(--space-1);
        }
        .compare-teaser__panel {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            align-items: start;
            padding: calc(var(--card-stripes-h) + var(--space-3)) var(--landing-inset) var(--space-3);
        }
        .compare-link {
            justify-content: center;
            width: 100%;
            white-space: normal;
        }
    }
</style>
